speechtext:
I
would like to ask the government if they consider it fair that the province of Nova Scotia, returning fourteen members, should have no representation on the committee. I appeal to the government and to the House, as a represenative of Nova Scotia;
I do not ask the province of Ontario to divide their representation with Nova Scotia, but I ask that a representative of that province be placed on the committee. Transportation in Nova Scotia is quite as important as in any other part of Canada, and perhaps more so, and any arrangement which would preclude a representative of Nova Scotia from having some insight into the workings of the railway is grossly unfair. Perhaps it is because Nova Scotia returned so large a proportion of Conservatives that my province is now being penalized.
